{
	"Name": "AlertQuery - Okta - User - Session - Okta User Session Impersonation",
	"Description": "An Okta administrator started, extended, or was granted an impersonation session. Impersonation lets an admin act as another user, and everything done inside the session is attributed to the impersonated account, so this is both a legitimate support tool and a very clean way to act as someone else.\n\nEvent types: user.session.impersonation.initiate, user.session.impersonation.grant, user.session.impersonation.extend, user.session.impersonation.revoke, user.session.impersonation.end\n\nReference(s):\n- https://detection.fyi/sigmahq/sigma/identity/okta/okta_user_session_impersonation/\n- https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/master/rules/identity/okta/okta_user_session_impersonation.yml",
	"GUID": "dc7485cb-e234-5d26-a5e7-261f1b7d8487",
